	(text "EXPANDER, I2C AND LEDS"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 20.32 17.78 0)
		(effects
			(font (size 2.5 2.5) (bold yes))
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "557e9d6b-6f01-5d0b-bf37-2a113163ebcf")
	)
	(text "TCA9555 at 0x20, M24C64 at 0x50; a Qwiic display is typically 0x3C/0x3D. 2.2 kΩ I2C pull-ups for 400 kHz.\nThe TCA9555 powers up with every line an input pulled high internally (~100 kΩ): switch enables and the gate\nOE are defined by the pulls on their own sheets. Buttons and switches use P07 and P10-P17: hole → 1 kΩ → node with\n10 kΩ to +3V3D and 100 nF (10 nF on SW5-SW8) → expander pin, as EuroPi does. A button pulls its hole to GND.\nENCODERS: wire A and B to gate inputs 3 and 4 (a clean comparator into a direct GPIO; encoder common to a +3V3D hole),\nnot to the expander: a busy OLED holds the shared I2C bus for ~23 ms and steps get lost. The push switch can use any SW hole."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 20.32 22.86 0)
		(effects
			(font (size 1.5 1.5))
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "550e702c-e8ed-5c09-9985-2753420550d1")
	)
